# requirements.in — source-of-truth dependency declarations.
#
# Run `make lock` (or `pip-compile --generate-hashes --resolver=backtracking
# -o requirements.lock requirements.in`) IN A PYTHON 3.11+ ENV to regenerate
# `requirements.lock` whenever this file changes. CI installs via
# `pip install --require-hashes -r requirements.lock` for reproducibility.
#
# Why a separate .in: requirements.txt is left in place for legacy callers
# (developers running `pip install -r requirements.txt` against a 3.10 env
# during transition). The .in is the canonical source the lock derives from.

